  "intro": {
    "en": "On a winter morning, there's a good chance the birds at your feeder are finches. They are seed-eaters, with a short, strong bill for cracking seeds, and the males are some of our most colourful birds.\n\nThat makes them a good group to practise on: the bill shape is the same, so you have to look at the colours. Red, yellow, green, black and white: one for each.\n\nAt the end there's a quiz of ten questions, with birds from the last two lessons mixed in."
  },
  "words": [
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "cone-shaped bill"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "A short, thick bill, shaped like a cone: handy for cracking seeds."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "face mask"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "A patch of a different colour around the bill, like a mask."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "chin"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "The part right under the bill, above the throat."
      }
    },
    {
      "term": {
        "en": "wing edge"
      },
      "explain": {
        "en": "The outer edge of the folded wing."
      }
    }
  ],
